{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-instanton","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:instanton","kind":"example","title":"Instanton connection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-c-quantum-universe","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-instanton"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-instanton","tags":["instanton","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.InstantonConnection","text":"instanton.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/instanton.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:instanton\"></a><p>To verify that the categorical formalism recovers the classical gauge-theoretic object, we specialise to the archimedean setting. In the archimedean quantum universe, a categorical instanton specialises to an <em>instanton connection</em> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">P</code>. This is a connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> whose curvature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A</code>, restricted to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H = \\ker\\varTheta</code>, is self-dual: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A|_H = {*_H}F_A|_H</code>. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Hodge star <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q</code> specialises to the Webster Hodge star <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">*_H</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^2 H^*</code>. Consequently, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q</code>-self-duality recovers classical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">*_H</code>-self-duality.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/instanton.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Example","number":"4.5.3"}
